  "//browserslist": [
    "Next ships its own browser target (MODERN_BROWSERSLIST_TARGET: chrome 64,",
    "edge 79, firefox 67, opera 51, safari 12) to the CSS pipeline. Declaring a",
    "postcss.config replaces that pipeline wholesale, and a bare autoprefixer",
    "then resolves browserslist on its own — falling back to `defaults`, which",
    "today means recent Safari and little else, so it emits no prefixes at all.",
    "The marketing CSS lost -webkit-backdrop-filter, -webkit-clip-path and",
    "-webkit-sticky the moment Tailwind was added, and nothing about the build",
    "said so: the glass nav pill and the mobile nav sheet simply stopped being",
    "frosted on Safari 17 and older. Pinning the same list here restores what",
    "Next was doing."
  ],
  "browserslist": [
    "chrome 64",
    "edge 79",
    "firefox 67",
    "opera 51",
    "safari 12"
  ],
  "devDependencies": {
    "@types/node": "^22.16.5",
    "@types/react": "^19.1.0",
    "@types/react-dom": "^19.1.0",
    "autoprefixer": "^10.4.21",
    "postcss": "^8.5.6",
    "tailwindcss": "^3.4.17",
    "typescript": "^5.8.3"
  }
